    "long_instructions": "## ECHO Framework\r\n\r\n#### The ECHO framework helps you compare code, build with AI, notice strong coding choices, and create your own final version.\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 900px; margin: auto;\">\r\n\r\n  <!-- E -->\r\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;\">\r\n    <img src=\"https://images.code.org/f6f049b0e8d02240d84d6429bee372b2-image-1774452696872.png\" alt=\"Letter E\" style=\"width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt;\">\r\n      <h3><b>Explore</b></h3>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Look at two different versions of a feature and compare how each one works.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 18px; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n        🔍 “What are two ways I could build a filter?”\r\n      </p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- C -->\r\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;\">\r\n    <img src=\"https://images.code.org/96e429722e4a63feae5fd5ce6e9c0324-image-1766176537283.png\" alt=\"Letter E\" style=\"width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt;\">\r\n      <h3><b>Co-Create</b></h3>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Build the feature with AI by asking questions, testing ideas, and making changes together.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 18px; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n        🤝 “Help me make this filter work step by step.”\r\n      </p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- H -->\r\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;\">\r\n    <img src=\"https://images.code.org/b86b54fc92932e1f8d7620d3fb6b9de5-image-1766176588734.png\" alt=\"Letter H\" style=\"width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt;\">\r\n      <h3><b>Highlight</b></h3>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Point out the best practices you notice from both versions of the code.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 18px; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n        ✨ “What makes these filter solutions strong?”\r\n      </p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <!-- O -->\r\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;\">\r\n    <img src=\"https://images.code.org/fdbfe39571b2275c717bc544798f12d0-image-1774452648029.png\" alt=\"Letter O\" style=\"width: 20%; max-width: 120px; height: auto; border-radius: 12px;\">\r\n    <div style=\"flex: 1; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt;\">\r\n      <h3><b>Own</b></h3>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Write your own version of the feature so the final code reflects your understanding.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 18px; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">\r\n        💻 “Now I’ll build my own filter pattern.”\r\n      </p>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n## Applying the ECHO Framework\r\n\r\n#### Students will use the ECHO framework to study filter patterns by comparing examples, building with AI, identifying good coding practices, and then creating their own solution.\r\n\r\n#### This process helps students learn from examples without copying blindly. Instead, they test ideas, reflect on what works, and use that understanding to write code independently.\r\n\r\n#### As students work with larger data sets and more advanced programs, a process like ECHO can help them use AI as a learning partner while still taking ownership of their code.\r\n\r\n## Try it out\r\n\r\n#### Watch the video below to see a walk through of using the ECHO framework in the next activity, where you will wok with AI to make a filter. "
  },
